  (text "Row 1, pins 1-7 (front row, under the housing)\n1  GND (battery negative)\n2  GND (sensor / UART / RS485 return)\n3  UART TX (3.3 V out)\n4  UART RX (5 V tolerant in)\n5  RS485 A\n6  DIN COM = VEH_GND (isolated DIN return)\n7  DIN COM = VEH_GND (second return wire)"
    (at 25.4 45.72 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "3c090c91-bd15-4df7-be91-50f5b667d69d")
  )
  (text "Row 2, pins 8-14 (back row)\n8   VIN 9-30 V (inline 1 A fuse at the battery)\n9   AIN1 0-30 V (4-20 mA with R904 fitted)\n10  DOUT1 open drain, 0.5 A (load from +V to pin 10)\n11  +5 V out, 200 mA (F801), for UART / AIN sensors\n12  RS485 B\n13  DIN1 (alternator L / D+ or oil-pressure switch)\n14  DIN2 (pulse input)"
    (at 116.84 45.72 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "e0c0405d-8031-410e-97e4-4fb07c3f2947")
  )
  (text "Pin order: the five vehicle-voltage nets (VIN, AIN1, DOUT1, DIN1, DIN2) sit on the back row and leave the header straight back.\nTheir 0.8 mm Vehicle clearance leaves no room for a track between two of them (the pad gap is 1.5 mm), so each front-row signal\nleaves between a back-row pin pair that holds at most one vehicle net. The isolated DIN group (6, 7, 13, 14) fills the pin 7/14 end,\nnext to the DIN island; its neighbours are RS485 A/B (5/12), which are rated +/-70 V.\nNot isolated: GND is the vehicle ground. Only DIN1/DIN2 are isolated; their return is pin 6 or 7, never a GND pin."
    (at 25.4 71.12 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "918348f6-2808-4f26-95f7-f7f2e95a8430")
  )
